// ============================================================================================
// MOH Trilogy Coop - PROTOTYPE A "CINEMATIC" - main page.        PROTOTYPE. NOT A SHIPPING MENU.
//
// WHAT THIS IS
//   A layout study for a main menu built like a title card: one full-bleed plate carrying the
//   image, and a short, quiet column of large items down the left edge over a soft gradient.
//   Nothing is crowded and nothing is boxed - the only "panel" is the darkness itself.
//   Five items, one caption line, one dev hint.  That is the whole page.
//
//   The plate ("coop_proto_a_backplate", the FIRST resource below) is deliberately the only
//   widget that carries the image, so the backdrop can be swapped for something else later -
//   a still, or an in-engine render of a map location - by pointing one cvar at it and
//   touching nothing else on the page.
//
// HOW TO OPEN IT  (nothing under ui/proto/ is loaded until you ask for it - see WHY, below)
//     exec ui/proto/coop_proto_a.cfg           <- does all of the following for you
//   or by hand, from the console (~):
//     loadmenu proto/coop_proto_a_ops
//     loadmenu proto/coop_proto_a_main
//     pushmenu coop_proto_a_main
//   BACK (bottom left, from the shared chrome) is popmenu 0 - it returns you to whatever menu
//   was underneath, normally the real main menu.  No shipped menu is touched or shadowed.
//
// WHY IT CANNOT DISTURB THE REAL MENUS
//   The startup sweep is FS_ListFiles("ui/", "urc", qfalse, &nfiles) at client/cl_ui.cpp:5634.
//   wantSubs=qfalse makes the pak walk reject any entry whose path depth != 1
//   (qcommon/files.cpp:2426), so ui/proto/*.urc is never enumerated and never auto-registered.
//   A prototype exists only after an explicit loadmenu.  Every menu name here is also
//   coop_proto_-prefixed, and menu names are a single global namespace, so even a hand load
//   cannot collide with a shipped menu.
//
// CONTAINER: fullscreen 1.  DELIBERATE - here is the reasoning, since a cinematic page is
//   exactly where you would want the live 3D world showing through:
//     * A non-fullscreen menu does let the world render behind it (client/cl_ui.cpp:1993-2005:
//       a fullscreen menu calls view3d->setShow(false) and Com_FakePause()s a running server;
//       a non-fullscreen one shows the view while clc.state == CA_ACTIVE).
//     * BUT the shared chrome's first widget, "coop_proto_bleed", is a stretch-both Widget
//       with bgcolor alpha 1.00, and uilib/uiwidget.cpp:2056 paints any bgcolor whose alpha is
//       non-zero across the whole rect.  It covers the entire physical screen, first, opaquely.
//       Declaring fullscreen 0 would therefore buy a 3D scene that is 100% occluded, and would
//       un-pause the server while you stare at a menu.
//   So: fullscreen 1 while the chrome owns an opaque ground.  The day the backdrop becomes a
//   live map view, the change is (a) fullscreen 0 here and (b) an alpha on the chrome's bleed -
//   the column, the mattes and the gradient below all keep working unmodified.
//
// ENGINE RULES THIS FILE IS BUILT AROUND (each re-verified against openmohaa-hzm)
//   * Widgets DO NOT NEST.  Every resource is a direct child of the menu container
//     (uilib/uilayout.cpp:150).  This is a flat list; the "column" is a shared x and a rhythm
//     of y values, nothing more.
//   * Draw order is DECLARATION order, and hit-testing walks children LAST to FIRST
//     (uilib/uiwidget.cpp:1721-1745).  So: plate, then gradient, then mattes, then text, then
//     the click targets last.  ordernumber is arrow-key focus order only (uiwidget.cpp:1506).
//   * "stretch horizontal" is a PROPERTY, not a resource type (uiwidget.cpp:347 -> handler
//     LayoutStretch at :1409-1422).  It sets pos.x = 0 and width = uid.vidWidth
//     (:1142-1145, :2288-2291) AND sets WF_NOPARENTADJUST|WF_DIRECTED, which makes the widget
//     screen-absolute and skips the parent-clip intersection at :872-906.  That is what lets
//     the plate and the two mattes run past the 640-wide canvas to the real edges of an
//     ultrawide instead of being pillarboxed.  It has zero uses in retail data.
//   * There is NO text wrapping - only a literal \n breaks a line (uilib/uifont.cpp:388-428).
//     Every title below is one line, sized against the measured metrics: facfont-20 is about
//     8.5 px per capital (11 px worst case, "W"); verdana-12 about 5.6; courier-16 exactly 8.
//   * "textalign" reads ONLY its first argument - the loop at uiwidget.cpp:1510-1529 calls
//     ev->GetString(1) on every pass regardless of the index.  "textalign left centery" would
//     silently apply "left" twice, so each value gets its own line.
//   * The default borderstyle is border_indent, NOT none (uiwidget.cpp:747), and "RAISED" -
//     used 40 times across this mod shipped UI - is not a recognised value (:1349-1360) and
//     silently leaves that indent border drawn.  Every widget here says borderstyle "NONE".
//   * A Button prints its title with its own font/fgcolor (uilib/uibutton.cpp:229-238), and
//     hovershader is drawn BEFORE that text (uiwidget.cpp:2110-2117, then Draw() at :2119) -
//     so the highlight lands behind the label on the same widget, no second resource needed.
//     "name" does NOT set the title (uiwidget.cpp:1324-1327); only "title" does.
//   * "enabledcvar" draws and hit-tests purely off the cvar: UI_GetCvarInt(name, 0) != 0
//     (uiwidget.cpp:1709, gate at :2027), and a gated-off widget is click-transparent
//     (:1730-1739).  An unset cvar reads 0, so the hover marks below are hidden until hovered.
//   * A backslash-quote inside a quoted token is a literal quote and does not end the token
//     (qcommon/script.cpp:907-929) - that is how the hovercommands set a captioned string.
//   * Every field is on its OWN LINE: a single-line resource block is silently dropped.
//
// ASSETS - all pre-existing and confirmed present.  No new shader is declared (bug-922: a
// bare-name shader for new menu art cost five sessions), no invented font (an unloadable font
// name is Com_Error(ERR_DROP) at uilib/uifont.cpp:295-299 - the client drops at menu load):
//     fonts       facfont-20, verdana-12, courier-16   (the only three used anywhere in this mod)
//     shaders     menu_button_trans, textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight
//                 (both shipped, and used exactly this way in ui/multiplayerstart.urc:174-176)
//     sounds      sound/menu/apply.wav   (sound/menu/mouseover.wav does NOT exist)
//     backdrop    none by default - see coop_protoAArt in ui/proto/coop_proto_a.cfg
//
// WIRING - everything here is inert and reversible.  Two items push the sibling prototype page
// (coop_proto_a_ops); three set a display-only cvar so the click visibly does something.
// Nothing loads a map, disconnects, quits, or writes a config.
// ============================================================================================

menu "coop_proto_a_main" 640 480 NONE 0
bgcolor 0 0 0 1
borderstyle NONE
bgfill 0 0 0 1
fullscreen 1
virtualres 1

include "ui/proto/coop_proto_chrome.inc"


// ============================================================================================
// THE PLATE - the one swappable backdrop widget.
// "stretch horizontal" spans the full physical width at any aspect while keeping the y band
// the rest of the page is composed against.  With coop_protoAArt unset it registers no
// material (uilib/uilabel.cpp:275-284) and simply shows its own colour, so the page is
// correct with no art at all.  It carries no title, so nothing prints over the image.
// ============================================================================================
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_backplate"
	rect 0 72 640 360
	stretch horizontal
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.070 0.078 0.068 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	linkcvar "coop_protoAArt"
	linkcvartoshader
}

// --- gradient off the left edge -------------------------------------------------------------
// Three stepped alphas stand in for a gradient: the column has to stay legible over whatever
// image lands on the plate, and there is no gradient primitive.  These are ordinary widgets,
// so they scale with the 640x480 design space rather than bleeding - only the plate and the
// mattes bleed, which is what keeps the composition anchored on an ultrawide.
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_grad1"
	rect 0 72 300 360
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.015 0.017 0.014 0.78
	borderstyle "NONE"
}
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_grad2"
	rect 300 72 90 360
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.015 0.017 0.014 0.50
	borderstyle "NONE"
}
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_grad3"
	rect 390 72 84 360
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.015 0.017 0.014 0.22
	borderstyle "NONE"
}

// --- letterbox mattes -----------------------------------------------------------------------
// The cinematic frame, and the practical reason for it: both mattes are "stretch horizontal",
// so on a 21:9 display they run to the physical edges while the plate image does too.  They
// also give the kicker (top) and the corner mark (bottom) a guaranteed dark band to sit on.
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_matte_top"
	rect 0 72 640 18
	stretch horizontal
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.010 0.010 0.010 0.62
	borderstyle "NONE"
}
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_matte_bot"
	rect 0 414 640 18
	stretch horizontal
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.010 0.010 0.010 0.62
	borderstyle "NONE"
}


// ============================================================================================
// TITLE BLOCK - drawn over the chrome sign plate.
// The chrome own title/strapline are cvar-driven and blank unless you set coop_protoTitle /
// coop_protoSub; this page carries fixed text instead, declared after the include so it draws
// on top.  Leave those two cvars unset for this prototype or the two will stack.
// "MOH TRILOGY COOP" at facfont-20 is 16 caps, about 136 px in a 460 px rect.
// ============================================================================================
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_title"
	title "MOH TRILOGY COOP"
	rect 90 16 460 24
	fgcolor 0.95 0.90 0.76 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign centerx
	outlinedtext 1
	dontlocalize
}
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_sub"
	title "the whole campaign, together"
	rect 90 42 460 15
	fgcolor 0.80 0.72 0.54 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign centerx
	dontlocalize
}

// --- column head ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_kicker"
	title "OPERATIONS"
	rect 36 74 264 14
	fgcolor 0.82 0.68 0.40 0.95
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign left
	dontlocalize
}
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_kickrule"
	rect 36 96 140 1
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.78 0.64 0.36 0.85
	borderstyle "NONE"
}


// ============================================================================================
// THE COLUMN.  Five items, 44 px apart, 34 px tall.
// Each item is TWO resources, declared in this order:
//   1. a hover mark - a 3 px brass tick outside the text, gated on its own cvar, so it is
//      invisible (and click-transparent) until the item is hovered;
//   2. the item itself - one Button that owns its text, its highlight, its caption and its
//      action.  Declared after the mark, and last overall, so it takes the click.
// The Buttons are the only clickable things on the page.
// ============================================================================================

// --- 1. CONTINUE ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_mark1"
	rect 22 118 3 34
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.86 0.70 0.36 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	enabledcvar "coop_protoAH1"
}
resource
Button
{
	name "coop_proto_a_item1"
	title "CONTINUE"
	rect 36 118 280 34
	fgcolor 0.94 0.90 0.78 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign left
	textalign centery
	shader "menu_button_trans"
	hovershader "textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight"
	clicksound "sound/menu/apply.wav"
	hovercommand "set coop_protoAH1 1; set coop_protoACap \"resume where the squad stopped\""
	mouseawaycommand "set coop_protoAH1 0; set coop_protoACap \"\""
	stuffcommand "pushmenu coop_proto_a_ops"
	ordernumber 2
	dontlocalize
}

// --- 2. OPERATIONS --------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_mark2"
	rect 22 162 3 34
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.86 0.70 0.36 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	enabledcvar "coop_protoAH2"
}
resource
Button
{
	name "coop_proto_a_item2"
	title "OPERATIONS"
	rect 36 162 280 34
	fgcolor 0.94 0.90 0.78 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign left
	textalign centery
	shader "menu_button_trans"
	hovershader "textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight"
	clicksound "sound/menu/apply.wav"
	hovercommand "set coop_protoAH2 1; set coop_protoACap \"pick a campaign and a mission\""
	mouseawaycommand "set coop_protoAH2 0; set coop_protoACap \"\""
	stuffcommand "pushmenu coop_proto_a_ops"
	ordernumber 3
	dontlocalize
}

// --- 3. SQUAD -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_mark3"
	rect 22 206 3 34
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.86 0.70 0.36 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	enabledcvar "coop_protoAH3"
}
resource
Button
{
	name "coop_proto_a_item3"
	title "SQUAD"
	rect 36 206 280 34
	fgcolor 0.94 0.90 0.78 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign left
	textalign centery
	shader "menu_button_trans"
	hovershader "textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight"
	clicksound "sound/menu/apply.wav"
	hovercommand "set coop_protoAH3 1; set coop_protoACap \"loadout, appearance, service record\""
	mouseawaycommand "set coop_protoAH3 0; set coop_protoACap \"\""
	stuffcommand "set coop_protoAPick squad"
	ordernumber 4
	dontlocalize
}

// --- 4. SETTINGS ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_mark4"
	rect 22 250 3 34
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.86 0.70 0.36 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	enabledcvar "coop_protoAH4"
}
resource
Button
{
	name "coop_proto_a_item4"
	title "SETTINGS"
	rect 36 250 280 34
	fgcolor 0.94 0.90 0.78 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign left
	textalign centery
	shader "menu_button_trans"
	hovershader "textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight"
	clicksound "sound/menu/apply.wav"
	hovercommand "set coop_protoAH4 1; set coop_protoACap \"coop rules, audio, video\""
	mouseawaycommand "set coop_protoAH4 0; set coop_protoACap \"\""
	stuffcommand "set coop_protoAPick settings"
	ordernumber 5
	dontlocalize
}

// --- 5. CREDITS -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
resource
Widget
{
	name "coop_proto_a_mark5"
	rect 22 294 3 34
	fgcolor 1.00 1.00 1.00 1.00
	bgcolor 0.86 0.70 0.36 1.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	enabledcvar "coop_protoAH5"
}
resource
Button
{
	name "coop_proto_a_item5"
	title "CREDITS"
	rect 36 294 280 34
	fgcolor 0.94 0.90 0.78 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "facfont-20"
	textalign left
	textalign centery
	shader "menu_button_trans"
	hovershader "textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight"
	clicksound "sound/menu/apply.wav"
	hovercommand "set coop_protoAH5 1; set coop_protoACap \"who built this, and on whose work\""
	mouseawaycommand "set coop_protoAH5 0; set coop_protoACap \"\""
	stuffcommand "set coop_protoAPick credits"
	ordernumber 6
	dontlocalize
}


// ============================================================================================
// THE CAPTION - one line, driven by whichever item the mouse is over.  This is the whole
// reason the page can afford to be this sparse: the explanation lives here instead of under
// every item.  Empty when nothing is hovered (an unset/empty cvar prints nothing).
// Longest caption is 35 chars at verdana-12, about 196 px in a 300 px rect.
// ============================================================================================
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_caption"
	rect 36 344 300 14
	fgcolor 0.88 0.85 0.74 0.95
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign left
	linkcvar "coop_protoACap"
	dontlocalize
}

// --- click readout: proof the three cvar-setting items actually fired --------------------
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_picklabel"
	title "last action"
	rect 36 364 74 13
	fgcolor 0.60 0.57 0.50 0.85
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign left
	dontlocalize
}
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_pick"
	rect 112 364 200 13
	fgcolor 0.82 0.70 0.42 1.00
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign left
	linkcvar "coop_protoAPick"
	dontlocalize
}

// --- dev hint: names the one cvar that swaps the backdrop --------------------------------
// courier-16 is 8 px per character exactly, so 27 characters is 216 px in a 300 px rect.
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_hint"
	title "set coop_protoAArt <shader>"
	rect 36 384 300 16
	fgcolor 0.55 0.62 0.55 0.80
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "courier-16"
	textalign left
	dontlocalize
}

// --- corner mark, sitting in the bottom matte ---------------------------------------------
resource
Label
{
	name "coop_proto_a_corner"
	title "PROTOTYPE A / CINEMATIC"
	rect 380 416 244 14
	fgcolor 0.70 0.66 0.56 0.45
	bgcolor 0.00 0.00 0.00 0.00
	borderstyle "NONE"
	font "verdana-12"
	textalign right
	dontlocalize
}

end.
